# Bench: one K-type TC on an Adafruit AD8495 breakout, OUT -> AIN10 (J5 pad 6), Vin -> J2 pad 1, GND -> J5 GND.
# 2026-10-20 boil read 95.3 C vs 99.8 (a bare-Teensy rig read the same probe ~93 C). Bias reset to 0 until the cause
# is known. Suspected, not confirmed: the TC plug reached the amp through breadboard + copper jumpers, which would move
# the cold junction to the steam-warmed plug. Check: squeeze the plug for 30 s at room temp, the reading must not move.
# Probe: K-TEST (bench test probe, no serial, not a flight sensor). Any bias here is NOT a flight calibration.
configs { channel: 10  assignment: TC002  tc_type: K_TYPE  tc_bias_deg_c: 0 }
